= Layers user guide =
Documentation reviewed September 6, 2026 for version 1.5.95 and subsequent fixes on main. Layers supports '''images, PDF pages and standalone slides'''.

== Start with the right content type ==
{| class="wikitable"
! Content !! Editor !! Embed example
|-
| Image || Open its File page and choose Edit Layers || <code><nowiki>[[File:Diagram.png|600px|layerset=annotations]]</nowiki></code>
|-
| Standalone slide || <code>Special:Slides</code> or <code>Special:EditSlide/SafetyProcedure</code> || <code><nowiki>{{#Slide: SafetyProcedure|size=800x600}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| PDF page || Open its File page, choose Edit Layers and select the document page || <code><nowiki>[[File:Manual.pdf|page=2|600px|layerset=annotations]]</nowiki></code>
|}
Create and save the content and named sets before using these examples. PDF annotation requires working PDF thumbnails (normally PdfHandler). Slides need no background image or PDF dependency.

== Select a named layer set ==
{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter !! Behavior
|-
| <code>layerset=on</code> || Select the current set; this is not necessarily a set named default
|-
| <code>layerset=default</code> || Request the set literally named default
|-
| <code>layerset=annotations</code> || Request the set named annotations
|-
| <code>layerset=none</code> or <code>layerset=off</code> || Disable annotations
|}
The older <code>layers=</code> spelling remains supported. Prefer descriptive names; names resembling intent values such as on/off/1 have inconsistent handling on some paths.

<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext">
[[File:Diagram.png|thumb|400px|layerset=annotations|Equipment diagram]]
[[File:Diagram.png|600px|layerset=on|layerslink=lightbox]]
[[File:Diagram.png|600px|layerset=on|layerslink=editor-modal]]
{{#Slide: SafetyProcedure|canvas=1200x800|size=800x600|layerset=instructions}}
{{#Slide: SafetyProcedure|size=800x600|noedit}}
</syntaxhighlight>

For slides, <code>canvas=</code> controls creation dimensions; <code>size=</code> controls display dimensions. <code>noedit</code> hides an edit button, not API authorization. Editor-modal viewing requires compatible same-origin framing settings; see the installation/configuration guide.

== Basic editing ==
# Add textboxes, callouts, shapes or other drawing layers.
# Use the Pointer tool to select, move, resize and rotate them.
# Choose a descriptive set name, then save.
# View the saved result in the article and lightbox.

Use Ctrl+Z for undo, Ctrl+Y or Ctrl+Shift+Z for redo, 0 to fit, +/- to zoom, and Space-drag to pan. Keyboard behavior inside text fields differs from canvas commands. The editor's keyboard help is the reference for available commands.

When editing a multi-page PDF, unsaved pages are held in memory. Save writes changed pages individually; this is not an atomic document save. Failed saves leave work unsaved. Keep the editor open and retry before closing the browser. Review recovery drafts before accepting them.

== Permissions and retention ==
The <code>editlayers</code> right controls editing. File annotations also require the applicable File-page editing authority. Deletion/renaming requires creator ownership or <code>layers-admin</code>; ordinary <code>delete</code> is not the override. Document-wide changes check every affected PDF page's set.

New revisions preserve server-generated creator metadata. Legacy sets whose creator evidence was pruned require an administrator for deletion/renaming. Layers normally retains 50 revisions per set/document page; these are '''not MediaWiki article revisions'''. Deleting a set removes its retained data.

== SOPs, search and Cargo ==
Standalone slides can hold visual instructions, but current Layers saves do not reliably create history entries on their embedding article. The legacy history-tracking option does not fix this. Annotation text is not explicitly indexed by ordinary MediaWiki search; slide-name and editor-layer filters are different.

Cargo galleries can choose a set from a query-result field. Textbox field bindings and Cargo tables containing annotation text are not implemented. The agreed development order is '''page revision history, MediaWiki search, then Cargo query/filter support'''.

== Export and troubleshooting ==
Client-side image export and lightbox print/download are separate from server PDF export. Server rendering and failed-page handling have known limitations; inspect important output against the viewer. Old server export cache entries may need regeneration after updating to the source-title binding fix.

If something fails, record the branch/commit, content type, markup, browser and sanitized API/console errors. Never post confidential SOP text or tokens to public issues.

